  "body": "In https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#downloading-resources we have an algorithm to determine a file name to use when a resource is being handled as a download. Currently for blob URLs that pretty much comes down to \" let filename have a value derived from the URL of the resource in a user-agent-defined manner\".\r\n\r\nI'm wondering if it makes sense to standardize a bit more in this area, and in particular to do what firefox does (or at least appears to do) when a blob URL was created from a `File` object. In that case it appears that firefox uses the `name` of the `File` object as filename for the download. That behavior seems pretty sensible, but not sure if this is something the spec should specify or if we're fine with just letting user agents do whatever they want in this area. In particular chrome currently doesn't do anything like this.",
